2026-04-30T21:36:26.063Z JOY-013A-CB comment.added "Plan: replace the manual 'Add: ...' note with an automatic User-PATH set. Use [Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('Path','User') to read the User-scope PATH (not :Path which mixes User+System), prepend  if not already present, and SetEnvironmentVariable('Path', ..., 'User'). Same fix in jyn.ps1. WM_SETTINGCHANGE is broadcast automatically. Print 'User PATH updated' line and a 'Restart your terminal' hint." [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
2026-04-30T21:36:26.198Z JOY-013A-CB item.status_changed "new -> in-progress" [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
2026-04-30T21:37:40.402Z JOY-013A-CB comment.added "[x] joy.ps1 and jyn.ps1: replaced the manual 'Note: ... Add: ...' hint with automatic User-PATH set. Reads User-scope PATH (not $env:Path which mixes User+System), checks idempotency by splitting on ';' (not substring match - avoids false positives if InstallDir is a prefix of another entry), prepends, writes back via SetEnvironmentVariable('Path', ..., 'User'). Prints 'User PATH updated' plus a 'Restart your terminal' hint. WM_SETTINGCHANGE is broadcast by SetEnvironmentVariable automatically. Linux/macOS sh installer untouched - automatic shell-rc modification would be invasive there." [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
